        "original_id": "8750aefb-e552-5b02-9b2b-b7d01a27c772",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tiburzio Spannocchi, Philip II of Spain, Philip III of Spain\n- Roles: king's engineer, monarch\n- Places: Spain, Portugal, Naples, Sicily, Sardinia, Milan\n\nFacts:\n- Tiburzio Spannocchi (1541–1609), also spelled Spanucchi, Spanochi, Spanoqui, and Hispanochi, served as king's engineer to Philip II of Spain and later to Philip III of Spain.\n- Philip III of Spain was born on 14 April 1578 and died on 31 March 1621.\n- Philip III of Spain was King of Spain.\n- Philip III of Spain also ruled as Philip II of Portugal, Naples, Sicily, and Sardinia, and he was Duke of Milan.",
